<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Togidubnus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1st century CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a> · Also known as Cogidubnus, Tiberius Claudius Togidubnus</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Togidubnus was a British client king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> in the 1st century CE who ruled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/regni">Regni</a>, in modern Sussex and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hampshire">Hampshire</a>, after the conquest of 43. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tacitus">Tacitus</a> says he stayed loyal to Rome, and an inscription at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chichester">Chichester</a> calls him <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tiberius">Tiberius</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/claudius">Claudius</a> Togidubnus, great king in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>. The palace at Fishbourne is often, though not certainly, linked with him.</p></div>
